<article class="env-lemma" id="0CKR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0CKR">Lemma <span data-tag="0CKR">15.107.1</span>.</a> Let $K$ be a field. If $B$ is weakly étale over $K$, then </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$B$ is reduced, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$B$ is integral over $K$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
any finitely generated $K$-subalgebra of $B$ is a finite product of finite separable extensions of $K$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$B$ is a field if and only if $B$ does not have nontrivial idempotents and in this case it is a separable algebraic extension of $K$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
any sub or quotient $K$-algebra of $B$ is weakly étale over $K$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
if $B'$ is weakly étale over $K$, then $B \otimes _ K B'$ is weakly étale over $K$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Part (1) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/092I" data-tag="092I">15.106.8</a> but of course it follows from part (3) as well. Part (3) follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/092Q" data-tag="092Q">15.106.16</a> and the fact that étale $K$-algebras are finite products of finite separable extensions of $K$, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00U3" data-tag="00U3">10.143.4</a>. Part (3) implies (2). Part (4) follows from (3) as a product of fields is a field if and only if it has no nontrivial idempotents. 
    <p>
      If $S \subset B$ is a subalgebra, then it is the filtered colimit of its finitely generated subalgebras which are all étale over $K$ by the above and hence $S$ is weakly étale over $K$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/092Q" data-tag="092Q">15.106.16</a>. If $B \to Q$ is a quotient algebra, then $Q$ is the filtered colimit of $K$-algebra quotients of finite products $\prod _{i \in I} L_ i$ of finite separable extensions $L_ i/K$. Such a quotient is of the form $\prod _{i \in J} L_ i$ for some subset $J \subset I$ and hence the result holds for quotients by the same reasoning. 
    <p>
      The statement on tensor products follows in a similar manner or by combining Lemmas <a href="/tag/092H" data-tag="092H">15.106.7</a> and <a href="/tag/092J" data-tag="092J">15.106.9</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>